# Copy to `.env` and run `npm run db:up` first.
#
# These values are safe to commit because they are LOCAL ONLY: the portal has no
# production environment and is deliberately never deployed, so this password
# protects a container bound to this machine. Nothing here belongs in Secrets
# Manager, and nothing here is a real credential.

# Postgres from docker-compose.yml. Port 55432, not 5432 -- this machine
# already runs other Postgres containers, and a clash reads as "the database is
# broken" rather than "something else has that port".
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://howto:howto-local-only@localhost:55432/howto?schema=public"

# Prisma wants both. There is no connection pooler in front of this one, so they
# are the same -- but the schema declares `directUrl`, and omitting it fails at
# `prisma validate` with "Environment variable not found", not at connect time.
DATABASE_DIRECT_URL="postgresql://howto:howto-local-only@localhost:55432/howto?schema=public"

# There is deliberately NO test-database variable here.
#
# The integration and E2E tiers run against `howto_test`, derived from the URL
# above by appending `_test` and created on demand -- see
# src/lib/db/testDatabaseUrl.ts. A variable would be a thing to forget, and what
# forgetting it falls back to is the database the portal serves: the integration
# tier wipes every table in `beforeEach`, ran that way for its whole life, and
# left its last fixture behind as the portal's entire contents for five days.
# Deriving means a tier that connects at all connects somewhere safe.

# Signs the session cookie. At least 32 characters; the app REFUSES to start
# without it rather than falling back to a default, because a signing key with a
# known value is not a signing key and the failure is silent -- everything works
# and anybody can mint a session.
SESSION_SECRET="local-development-session-secret-not-a-real-key"
